<title>THAILAND: Thailand exempts jewellery from value added tax.</title>
<headline>Thailand exempts jewellery from value added tax.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai cabinet on Tuesday waived a 10 percent value added tax (VAT) on imports and sales of jewellery as part of a government policy to promote the industry and make Thailand a jewellery industry centre.</p>
<p>A government spokesman said at a news conference the VAT exemption for both natural and artificial jewellery would also create jobs in the industry.</p>
<p>The Thai government raised VAT to 10 percent from seven on August 16.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
